Promise.all() in TypeScript 🚀
Pichhle lesson mein humne Promise aur async/await seekha. Ab seekhenge ki multiple asynchronous tasks ko ek saath kaise run karte hain.
1. Problem samjho
Maan lo tumhe 3 APIs se data lena hai:
- Users API
- Products API
- Orders API
Agar ek-ek karke await karoge:
const users = await getUsers();
const products = await getProducts();
const orders = await getOrders();


Toh har call agle call se pehle complete hogi. Agar har API ko 2 seconds lagen, toh total lagbhag 6 seconds lag sakte hain.
2. Promise.all() use karo
async function main() {
  const [users, products, orders] = await Promise.all([
    getUsers(),
    getProducts(),
    getOrders()
  ]);

  console.log(users);
  console.log(products);
  console.log(orders);
}


Ye calls ek saath start hoti hain. Agar teeno ko 2 seconds lagen, toh total time lagbhag 2 seconds ho sakta hai, na ki 6 seconds.
